   "notes": "Preferred default for mantle work. The fit combines multi-anvil data at 28-63 GPa and 300-1500 K with laser-heated DAC data at 52-108 GPa and 300 or 1500-2430 K; the study reports measurements up to 110 GPa and 2500 K. V0=162.373 A^3 was fixed to an independent ambient measurement; theta0=950(150) K, gamma0=1.54(9), and q=1.5(3). The paper calls the exponent b; with its fixed a=1, the published Gruneisen expression reduces exactly to gamma=gamma0(V/V0)^b used here.",
